<title>USA: Boise Cascade Corp Q4 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Boise Cascade Corp Q4 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dec. 31, 1996     Q4     Dec. 31, 1995</p>
<p> Shr primary loss	 $0.16   profit	 $1.15</p>
<p> Shr diluted loss	 $0.16   profit	  1.07</p>
<p> Net			  2,140		   70,240</p>
<p> Revs		   1,262,740		1,241,960</p>
<p>					    YEAR</p>
<p> Shr primary loss	 $0.63   profit	 $5.93</p>
<p> Shr diluted loss	  0.63   profit	  5.39</p>
<p> Net			  9,050		  351,860</p>
<p> Revs		   5,108,220		5,074,230</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	48,277		   55,028</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	48,277		   61,351</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income figures exclude preferred dividend payments, whereas per share figures include preferred dividend payments.</p>
<p>Q4 1996 includes several one-time transactions resulting in a net increase to net income of $10.7 million, or $0.22 per fully diluted share.</p>
<p>1995 also includes several one-time adjustments that increased net income by $15.1 million and fully diluted earnings per share $0.25 for the year.</p>
<p>Fully diluted net loss for the three months and year ended December 31, 1996, was antidilutive; therefore, the amounts reported for primary and fully diluted loss are the same.</p>
</text>
